Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with its specialized agents, is pleased to submit a tender proposal for the implementation of an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions for the City of Belval. Our proposed solution leverages our expertise in Large Language Models (LLMs), Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities, and our commitment to sovereignty, security, and sustainability. We aim to provide a comprehensive, user-friendly, and efficient tool that integrates with existing systems, enhances information access, improves answer quality, and reduces processing times.

# 2. Understanding of Requirements
We have carefully reviewed the call for tenders issued by the City of Belval and understand the need for an intelligent assistance tool accessible from the agents' work environment. This tool must facilitate information search, provide drafting help, assist in file instruction, suggest actions or steps within administrative processes, and ensure seamless integration with existing practices and systems without disrupting current workflows.

# 3. Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution integrates the contributions of all our specialized agents to meet the City's requirements comprehensively. 

**Technical Architecture**: We will utilize OVHcloud or Scaleway as our cloud provider, ensuring EU-based hosting that meets sovereignty constraints. Our technical architecture will leverage Docker and Kubernetes (K8s) for efficient deployment and scaling, achieving a response time of less than 2 seconds and 99.9% availability. For API integration with civil-status software, town-planning systems, EDM, and user directories, we will use API standards like REST and GraphQL, along with Kong as the API gateway.

**Security and Compliance**: To ensure GDPR compliance, we will guarantee EU-only hosting, prevent data transfers outside the EU, protect sensitive data through encryption (utilizing tools such as Microsoft Presidio for anonymization), and implement a human oversight mechanism to validate automated decisions. Our Data Protection Officer will oversee these processes, aligning with our ISO 27001 certification.

**AI Innovation**: We propose leveraging our Large Language Model, Mistral 7B Instruct, fine-tuned using LoRA or QLoRA methods for high-quality answers and suggestions in administrative tasks. Our RAG capabilities will enable efficient information retrieval from internal procedures and applicable regulations. Quantization methods like INT8 will optimize model performance while minimizing energy consumption.

**Budget**: With a maximum contract value eligibility of €3,000,000, we meet the project's budget requirement. We aim for a target gross margin percentage of 28%, ensuring cost optimization through efficient resource allocation and potential rate renegotiation with subcontractors if needed. Our standard daily rates and infrastructure margin will guide our pricing strategy.

**Sustainability**: To minimize environmental footprint, we will utilize green hosting partners like OVHcloud or Scaleway, practice digital sobriety through model quantization (reducing GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%), auto-scaling, and query result caching. Our e-waste management partner, Ecologic, ensures responsible electronic waste disposal.

**Project Coordination**: We will manage the project using the PRINCE2 methodology, dividing it into four phases: Inception & Design, Pilot / MVP, Full Rollout, and Operations & Support. Each phase is designed to ensure successful deployment, user adoption, and long-term sustainability of the solution.

# 4. Unaddressed Requirements
Upon reviewing the call for tenders and our agents' answers, all specified requirements have been addressed in our proposal. However, we note that specific details on civil-status software, town-planning systems, EDM, and user directories would be necessary to finalize the technical design of API integrations.

# 5. Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with its specialized agents, is confident in its ability to deliver a comprehensive artificial intelligence solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements for assisting municipal agents. Our proposed solution integrates cutting-edge technology, robust security measures, and sustainable practices, ensuring not only the efficiency and effectiveness of administrative services but also compliance with regulatory frameworks and minimal environmental impact. We look forward to the opportunity to discuss our proposal in further detail and explore how we can contribute to the City's digital transformation strategy.
